  rtl/scroller.v         the 2048 character scroller with the zoom envelope (its text is in C64 screen codes)    copied unchanged
  rtl/screen_matrix.v    the 44 x 25 text screen                                                                   copied unchanged
  rtl/video_pattern.v    the picture: zoomed XOR luma, hue ramp, text overlay, the PAL subcarrier                   copied unchanged; NOT built (see below)

CHANGED (CC BY 4.0 asks that changes are marked):
  trx/ddt_novic_video.v  his video_pattern.v with the analogue back end replaced: his luma, his hue ramp and his saturation (44) become an RGB colour (the colour that a PAL receiver
                         with the nominal burst shows for them) instead of luma + a modulated 4.43 MHz subcarrier with burst, sync, blanking and line alternation; the sample coordinate is
                         the pixel column times two (his line counted 704 samples, two to a pixel); the vertical position is the picture line. The zoom background with its two dividers,
                         the text overlay, the hue ramp and the scroller connection are as he wrote them. rtl/video_pattern.v.diff is the difference.

NOT here, on purpose: top.v, video_timing.v, clock_gen_rmii_to_13m5.v (the MMCM, the THS8136 interface and the PAL raster are replaced by trx/); c64_chargen_ucg.hex and c64_font_rom.sv
(the C64 character ROM is Commodore's and never goes into this repository, a bench, a package or a .cor; the Mandelbrot core's trx/c64_font_rom.v keeps the module's name and ports and reads
Gideon's overlay font that the host already carries, host/mem/ovl_font8.mem; the glyphs look like that font, not like the C64's); C64U.xdc (Gideon's pin constraints); the .bit file, the
video and the images of his repository.

What is ours (GPL v3, as the rest of this repository): layer2_ddt_novic.v, trx/ (ddt_novic_core.v, ddt_novic_video.v) and sim/; the register block, raster, frame writer and font module are
the Mandelbrot core's trx/ (cores/ddt_mandel/NOTICE).

